Copper clad laminate (CCL) is a foundational material used to manufacture printed circuit boards. It combines a resin-based substrate with copper foil to provide mechanical strength and electrical pathways required for modern electronic systems. Growing requirements for high-frequency transmission, miniaturization, thermal performance and environmental compliance are encouraging manufacturers to develop increasingly advanced laminate formulations.

